  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Three degrees of distance",
     "texto": [
      "In Spanish, we express physical distance using three sets of demonstratives:\n- **este / esta**: near the speaker (*este café*, *esta mesa*).\n- **ese / esa**: near the listener or at a middle distance (*ese camarero*, *esa silla*).\n- **aquel / aquella**: far from both speaker and listener (*aquel café*, *aquella terraza*).\n\nDemonstratives always agree in gender and number with the noun and in modern spelling take no written accent whether alone or before a noun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Agreement and spatial distance",
     "texto": [
      "Remember:\n- **este** (m.) and **esta** (f.) denote proximity to the speaker.\n- **aquel** and **aquella** indicate distance from both interlocutors."
     ],
